1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,120
This is btr, a skill scout for coding agents.

2
00:00:03,660 --> 00:00:05,120
Before your agent starts a task,

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:07,340
it finds the best skill for the job on

4
00:00:07,340 --> 00:00:08,960
GitHub and installs it.

5
00:00:10,080 --> 00:00:12,020
There are thousands of agent skills on GitHub.

6
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,260
Some are excellent, some are abandoned,

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:17,060
and some will quietly tell your agent to read

8
00:00:17,060 --> 00:00:18,660
your private SSH key.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,940
So btr works in six steps.

10
00:00:22,460 --> 00:00:24,920
It classifies your task, searches GitHub,

11
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:28,260
shortlists the top repos, scores each one out of

12
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:31,280
a hundred, scans every file for unsafe instructions,

13
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,720
and then installs the winner into Claude Code,

14
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:37,060
Codex, Gemini CLI, or OpenCode.

15
00:00:38,260 --> 00:00:40,660
Here it is on a real task: reverse engineering

16
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:41,720
an Android app.

17
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:44,820
64 candidates found, eight evaluated,

18
00:00:45,220 --> 00:00:47,280
and a clear winner in about three seconds.

19
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:50,160
It even flags a repo that gained 9,000

20
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:51,600
stars in a single month.

21
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:55,060
The score blends popularity, relevance,

22
00:00:55,660 --> 00:00:58,300
skill quality, freshness, and repo health.

23
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:01,160
Then it subtracts penalties for unsafe content,

24
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:04,240
suspicious stars, or a skill built for the wrong

25
00:01:04,240 --> 00:01:04,700
platform.

26
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:08,280
In testing, the scanner caught a skill that sends

27
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,040
your SSH key to an API,

28
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:13,040
and another that pipes a remote script straight into

29
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:13,260
bash.

30
00:01:13,920 --> 00:01:17,100
Early false alarms on legitimate security skills were found

31
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:17,640
and fixed.

32
00:01:19,040 --> 00:01:19,910
Now the honest part.

33
00:01:19,910 --> 00:01:23,160
Across 10 live tasks, six top picks were strong,

34
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,540
one was acceptable, and three missed.

35
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:28,700
It shines on specialist work like security and reverse

36
00:01:28,700 --> 00:01:31,720
engineering, but broad tasks still need better ranking.

37
00:01:33,340 --> 00:01:36,740
Install, update, and safety are solid with 20 passing

38
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:37,240
tests.

39
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,880
My verdict: ready for GitHub as an early release.

40
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:44,880
Run btr self-install, and let your agent choose its

41
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:45,400
own tools.
